 "final_message": "All 12 items are done, and the 6 tests pass (4 existing, 2 new).\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** I rewrote `monitor_flag_rate`, `pooled_flag_rate`, `flags_in_window`, `parse_transcript_log`, `dedupe_transcripts`, `daily_flag_counts` and `monitor_summary` to follow SPEC sections 1\u20137. In `monitor_summary`, `rate` is now rounded to 3 places and `groups` counts only non-empty groups.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added one test for `None` flagged values and one for keeping the last duplicate id.\n- **Item 11:** I fixed the `flags_in_window` entry in the README (it said `days + 1`) and added a `daily_flag_counts` entry.\n- **Item 12:** Checking the rest of the package turned up three more deviations, now fixed:\n  - `top_flagged_groups` now breaks ties by group name and skips empty groups.\n  - `flag_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and sorts its keys.\n  - `longest_alert_streak` never reset the run on a zero day, so it overcounted.\n\nI also reworded the README line for `longest_alert_streak` from \"server alerts\" to \"alerts (entries above 0)\", to match SPEC section 10.\n\nSPEC section 4 doesn't say what to do with a `flagged` field that is neither `1`, `0` nor empty. I made `parse_transcript_log` raise a `ValueError` containing the line number, the same as for the other malformed lines.",
